          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "шоколад (shokolád) — from Peter the Great's time. The ш- form came through German Schokolade, the old ч- form from Italian cioccolata; both go back to Spanish chocolate, from Nahuatl, the language of the Aztecs (Vasmer)."
            }
          ]
        },
